invalid.ts:2:42 lint/nursery/useExpectToHaveBeenCalledTimes  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  i toHaveLength() is used to check how many times a mock function was called.
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ expect((method as jest.Mock).mock.calls).toHaveLength(1);
      │                                          ^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ expect((<jest.Mock>method).mock.calls).toHaveLength(1);
    4 │ expect(method!.mock.calls).toHaveLength(1);
  
  i When this check fails, the error message describes the length of an array instead of the number of calls.
  
  i Use toHaveBeenCalledTimes() to check the number of calls.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use toHaveBeenCalledTimes() instead.
  
